editorial:
The only arithmetic operation is addition. Choosing the type matters: 2147483647 + 1 is a valid input whose answer is 2147483648. The possible sums range from −4294967296 to 4294967294, all representable in a signed 64-bit integer.

Read both operands as long long so the addition itself uses that type. Assigning a + b to a long long after adding two int operands would widen the result too late.
~~~
long long a, b;
cin >> a >> b;
cout << a + b << '\n';
~~~
This uses O(1) time and O(1) extra space.
